book><name>IBIDEN CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EN, HONJIN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIROSE, NAOHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IBIDEN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EN HONJIN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIROSE NAOHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EN, HONJIN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIROSE, NAOHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The insulation of an interlayer resin insulating layer (50) is not degraded since the mesh hole (35a) of an upper solid layer (35) is aligned with the mesh hole (59a) of an upper solid layer (59). The diameter of the mesh holes is preferably 75 to 300  mu m. If the diameter is below 75  mu m, it is difficult to align the holes; if the diameter is over 300  mu m, the insulation of the interlayer resin insulating layer degrades. The distance between the holes is preferably 100 to 2000  mu m. If the distance is below 100  mu m, the solid layers do not produce their functions; if the distance is over 2000  mu m, the insulation of the interlayer resin insulating layer degrades.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'alignement de la perforation de grille (35a) d'une couche supérieure solide (35) par rapport à la perforation de grille (59a) d'une autre couche supérieure solide (59) permet de ne pas altérer l'isolation d'une couche de résine intermédiaire isolante (50), le diamètre desdites perforations de grille variant de préférence entre 75 et 300  mu m. Néanmoins, si ce diamètre est inférieur à 75  mu m, ces perforations seront difficiles à aligner, et si ce diamètre est supérieur à 300  mu m, l'isolation de la couche de résine intermédiaire isolante est altérée, la distance séparant lesdites perforations variant par ailleurs de préférence entre 100 et 2000  mu m. Si cette distance est inférieure à 100  mu m, les couches solides ne pourront remplir leur fonction, et si cette distance dépasse 2000  mu m, l'isolation de ladite couche de résine intermédiaire isolante est altérée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>